A lighting shop tests inheritance with this fragment:
class Lamp { public String glow() { return "warm"; } }
class DeskLamp extends Lamp { }
DeskLamp d = new DeskLamp();
System.out.println(d.glow());
What is printed?

A gym tracks reps with this fragment:
class Counter { protected int n = 3; }
class StepCounter extends Counter { public void step() { n += 4; } public int read() { return n; } }
StepCounter s = new StepCounter();
s.step();
System.out.println(s.read());
What value is printed?

A box office premium ticket fails to compile here:
class Ticket { private double price = 12.0; }
class VipTicket extends Ticket { public double fee() { return price + 5; } }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A mailroom prices gift parcels with this fragment:
class Parcel { protected int w; public Parcel(int w) { this.w = w; } }
class GiftParcel extends Parcel { public GiftParcel(int w) { super(w); } public int ship() { return w * 2; } }
System.out.println(new GiftParcel(6).ship());
What value is printed?

A nature center extends bird calls with this fragment:
class Bird { public String call() { return "chirp"; } }
class Owl extends Bird { public String night() { return call() + "!"; } }
System.out.println(new Owl().night());
What is printed?

A sports club wires its coach roster with these classes:
class Member { protected String name; public Member(String name) { this.name = name; } }
class Coach extends Member { public Coach(String name) { _____; } }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A wildlife tracker fails to compile on this cub constructor:
class Bear { public Bear(int size) { } }
class Cub extends Bear { public Cub(int x) { size = x; super(x); } int size; }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A garage wants CarAlarm to replace the sound of this base class:
class Alarm { public String sound() { return "beep"; } }
class CarAlarm extends Alarm { _____ }
Which fragment correctly overrides the method?

A tile game sizes pieces with this fragment:
class Tile { public int area() { return 4; } }
class BigTile extends Tile { public int area() { return 9; } }
Tile t = new BigTile();
System.out.println(t.area() + new Tile().area());
What integer is printed?

An orchestra app plays instruments through this fragment:
class Instrument { public String play() { return "note"; } }
class Drum extends Instrument { public String play() { return "boom"; } }
Instrument i = new Drum();
System.out.println(i.play());
What is printed?

A kitchen scale surprises its maker by printing g500 instead of the expected kilograms:
class Scale { public String read(int grams) { return "g" + grams; } }
class SmartScale extends Scale { public String read(double grams) { return "kg" + grams; } }
SmartScale s = new SmartScale();
System.out.println(s.read(500));
Which statement explains the output?

A depot starter must start every vehicle in an array:
public static void startAll(Vehicle[] lot) { for (Vehicle v : lot) { _____; } }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A lobby kiosk greets guests through this fragment:
interface Greeter { String greet(); }
class Host implements Greeter { public String greet() { return "hello"; } }
Greeter g = new Host();
System.out.println(g.greet() + "?");
What is printed?

A geometry kit labels shapes with this fragment:
abstract class Shape { public abstract int sides(); public String tag() { return "s" + sides(); } }
class Tri extends Shape { public int sides() { return 3; } }
System.out.println(new Tri().tag());
What is printed?

A gift shop card fails to compile here:
interface Card { String label(); }
class GiftCard implements Card { String label() { return "gift"; } }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A race timer orders runners by finishing time with this class:
class Runner implements Comparable<Runner> {
  private int time;
  public Runner(int t) { time = t; }
  public int compareTo(Runner other) { _____; }
}
Which line orders faster times first?

A timing audit combines three comparisons of Runner objects ordered by time with return this.time - other.time;:
Runner a = new Runner(31), b = new Runner(47);
System.out.println(a.compareTo(b) + b.compareTo(a) + a.compareTo(a));
What integer is printed?

A depot prints routes only for buses with this fragment:
class Vehicle { }
class Bus extends Vehicle { public int routes() { return 12; } }
Vehicle v = new Bus();
if (v instanceof Bus) { System.out.println(((Bus) v).routes()); }
What value is printed?

A fare helper counts bus routes from any vehicle:
public static int busRoutes(Vehicle v) { if (_____) { return ((Bus) v).routes(); } return -1; }
Which guard belongs in the blank?

A rental desk crashes on this hopeful cast:
Vehicle v = new Vehicle();
Bus b = (Bus) v;
Which statement identifies the fault? Assume Bus extends Vehicle.

An arcade totals prize values with this fragment:
class Coin { public int value() { return 1; } }
class Token extends Coin { public int value() { return 5; } }
class Medal extends Token { public int value() { return 10; } }
Coin[] jar = {new Coin(), new Token(), new Medal(), new Token()};
int t = 0;
for (Coin c : jar) { t += c.value(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?
